// Subject: the game's damage model; game state only.
// The shell walk's angle laws at a face a round meets from air: ricochet, normalization and
// overmatch. Read by `src/ballistics/angle_laws.rs`, embedded and parsed once, validated at parse;
// applied by `ballistics::walk::begin`. The law and its inputs are design doc §4a,
// `.agents/docs/design/armor-penetration-and-damage.md`.
//
// Every law reads the same inputs: the round's hit-nose factor N (DERIVED at load from the
// `NoseShape` the force law reads: `assets/ballistics/round_types.ron`, or a round's own `nose`),
// its potency P at the face (the force law's readout at its speed there, metres of reference
// steel), and the crossing's factor-weighted thickness t along the face normal (metres of
// reference steel) over the calibre c of what meets the plate (a sub-calibre round's core). A new
// round type plugs in through its nose and carrier row; no law holds a per-type angle.
//
// The reference case every provisional value keeps is the 88 mm APCBC round (hit nose 1-crh
// ogive, N = 7/24) against a plate its potency just matches, P / t = 1: there it skids past 70° and
// straightens through 0.2 of its incidence, the values the walk carried from the serial resolver.
//
// PROVENANCE: every value is authored `(value, Kind("source or reason"))`, Kind names the value's job
// (`src/provenance.rs`); a value without one does not load.
(
    // Ricochet: a round that is not overmatched skids off when its incidence θ from the normal has
    // tan θ > grip × N × P / t. A blunter nose, a faster round and a thinner plate each raise the
    // critical angle; a plate far below the round's potency barely deflects it at all.
    ricochet_grip: (9.42, Unknown("no source in the repo gives a critical ricochet angle for any
        nose, speed or plate. Provisional, DERIVED: tan 70° / (7/24) = 9.4199, so the reference
        APCBC case keeps the 70° the walk carried. Settled by measured critical angles for at
        least two hit noses at two potency-to-thickness ratios")),
    // Normalization: a round that bites in straightens toward the normal through η × turn × N × θ
    // × (entrance factor / reference factor) of its incidence θ, η the disc's coverage. A blunter
    // nose turns further into the plate.
    normalization_turn: (0.685714304, Unknown("no source in the repo gives a normalization angle
        for any nose. Provisional, DERIVED: 0.2 / (7/24) = 0.685714…, authored as the f32 whose
        product with the f32 nose factor 7/24 is the f32 0.2, so the reference APCBC case keeps the
        0.2 share of its incidence the walk carried, to the bit. Settled by measured entry bends for
        at least two hit noses")),
    // Overmatch: a round whose calibre c is at least this × t neither skids nor pays the slope:
    // the plate is too thin to present its angle to it.
    overmatch_ratio: (3.0, Unknown("ASSUMED: carried from the serial resolver; no source in the
        repo gives the ratio. Settled by the calibre-to-thickness ratio past which measured
        oblique plates stop deflecting rounds and charging their slope")),
)
